# VOLT_CHECK_EXPECT_FAIL — `.method` outside a type body has no receiver.
#
# DotCallLowering rewrites it into `self.method`, and `self` is only bound
# inside a struct/class/enum/mixin body. A module is a namespace, not a type:
# its methods are registered as free functions, so they are called bare
# (`helper`), never through an implicit receiver.
#
# Expected: error: 'self' has no meaning outside a type body — a module is a
# namespace, not a type

.orphan_call
